  <p>
    Unlike a commercial bank clerk, an RBI Assistant does not sit at a customer-facing counter — RBI does
    not run retail branches for the public. The role is entirely internal: data entry, document
    verification, ledger reconciliation, and record-keeping that supports RBI's regulatory and currency
    operations. RBI Assistants also work a genuine five-day week, a structural benefit most bank clerical
    roles do not carry.
  </p>

