  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <p>
    Do not settle RBI and SBI career growth India from a relative's opinion or one salary comparison table
    for one more week.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      Run yourself through The 4-Checkpoint Protocol above, honestly, on paper.
    </p>
    <p>
      Then decide whether you are chasing policy-and-regulation work or commercial-banking-and-people work,
      and build your prep plan around one exam family as the primary target, so months of study time are not
      split thin across two genuinely different careers.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Achieving earlier financial freedom through either track depends more on which day-to-day work you can
    actually sustain and grow in for decades, not just which pay slip looks bigger this year. Move toward
    that decision with <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">career guidance</a>
    if you want a second opinion on your specific situation, or start with the free
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/assessments">career and skill assessments</a>
    if you are still unsure which working style genuinely fits you.
  </p>

  <p>
